f "/statistics/medal/country"} "Medals by country"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal/athlete"} "Medals by athlete"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal_table"} "Medal tables"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/participation"} "Participations"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/records"} "Olympic Records"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/age"} "Age records"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/age_at_death"} "Age at death"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/lists"} "Lists"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/today"} "Today"]] "\n" [:li {}] "\n" [:li {:class "divider"}] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics"} "Statistics"]] "\n"] "\n"] "\n\n\n\n\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/feedbacks/new"} "Feedback"]] "\n" [:form {:class "navbar-form navbar-left", :role "search", :action "/athletes/quick_search", :accept-charset "UTF-8", :method "post"} [:input {:name "utf8", :type "hidden", :value "✓", :autocomplete "off"}] [:input {:type "hidden", :name "authenticity_token", :value "havTZavtC4d9efa9QxBc0AX4P5nvTvfOAU2_V8cevpUjuShqk5Cu7MUWVnj9PluRIbMDXHm06bRH2IUEhchoIQ", :autocomplete "off"}] [:div {:class "form-group"} "\n" [:input {:type "text", :name "query", :id "query", :class "form-control", :placeholder "Athlete search"}] "\n"] "\n" [:input {:type "submit", :name "commit", :value "Go", :class "btn btn-default", :data-disable-with "Go"}] "\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "container"} "\n" [:ol {:class "breadcrumb"} "\n" [:li {} "\n" [:a {:href "/"} "Home"] "\n"] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/editions"} "Games"]] [:li {} [:a {:href "/editions/10"} "1932 Summer Olympics"]] [:li {} [:a {:href "/editions/10/sports/APN"} "Alpinism"]] [:li {:class "active"} "Alpinism, Open"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {} [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:span {} "No other events in this sport"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "900027"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "900062"} "1936"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/709"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Alpinism, Open" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "14 August 1932"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/300"} "Los Angeles Memorial Coliseum, Los Angeles, California"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/900056"} "2 from 1 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Sitting on the border of Switzerland and Italy, the Matterhorn was the last great Alpine peak to be successfully climbed, on 14 July 1865. But nobody had yet ascended via the north face of the mountain, via a huge wall. Two German brothers, who had cycled from München, decided to climb it, but had not publicly announced it. The two brothers, " [:a {:href "/athletes/901555"} "Franz"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/901556"} "Toni Schmid"] ", managed to master the rock wall, reaching the top on 1 August 1931. The " [:a {:href "/organizations/1"} "IOC"] " decided to award this performance with a gold medal during its session at the Los Angeles Olympics in 1932. German IOC member " [:a {:href "/athletes/899227"} "Theodor Lewald"] " accepted the prize in the absence of the two climbers. On 5 September 1932, Lewald handed out the prize in a special ceremony in München. The younger brother, Toni, had already died before the Los Angeles Olympics, falling to his death while attempting to climb the Wiesbachhorn, in the Austrian Hohe Tauern, so his medal was presented to their father. Toni was an educated construction engineer, and Franz became a police inspector in Neuhaus, in Schliersee."] "\n\n" [:p {} "At their trip to the Matterhorn in 1931, the Schmids had been accompanied by two friends, who decided at the last minute not to climb with them due to bad weather. Both of them would still find their place in Olympic history, though. Besides remaining a noted mountaineer, Hans Ertl became cameraman (and, allegedly, lover) of controversial and influential director Leni Riefenstahl. Among others, he was the chief cameraman for " [:em {} "Olympia"] ", her two-part masterpiece about the 1936 Olympics. Franz had also climbed the north face of the Ortler together with Hans Ertl, on 22 June 1931. At the 1936 Games, the fourth friend was also involved: " [:a {:href "/athletes/9942"} "Ernst Krebs"] " won a gold medal in the " [:a {:href "/results/255006"} "10,000 m K1"] " (kayak). In 1998, German journalist Imke Habegger described the ascent of the north wall in their article on 31 December, in the " [:em {} "General-Anzeiger"] " of Bonn: “Sleepless on the Icy Rock Needle. The Munich Brothers Franz and Toni Schmid Conquered the Dangerous North Face of the Matterhorn”."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/901555"} "Franz Schmid"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/901556"} "Toni Schmid"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:class "footnote", :href "#", :title "Awarded for the first ascent of Matterhorn North Face.", :data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right"} "1"]]]]] "\n"] "\n" [:footer {:class "footer"} "\n" [:br {}] "\n" [:div {:class "panel panel-info"} "\n" [:div {:class "panel-heading"} "\n" [:h3 {:class "panel-title"} "\n" [:span {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-info-sign"}] "\nDid you know?\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "panel-body"} "\n" [:p {} "The venues of the 1900 Olympics were not as advanced as today: the track and field events were held on a grass field scattered with trees, and swimming took place in the River Seine."] "\n\n\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "container"} "\n" [:p {} "\n" [:a {:href "/users/sign_in"} "Login"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/statistics/site"} "Statistics"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/static/about"} "About"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/static/faq"} "FAQ"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/feedbacks/new"} "Feedback"] "\n"] "\n" [:p {} "\n© " [:a {:href "/static/about"} "OlyMADMen"] " 2006 — 2026\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n\n" [:script {:src "/assets/lightbox.min-a06f7b5a37bdc88a78a48f95b9149ca917761a07bffb855a6d73c1a435e16552.js"}] #object[org.jsoup.nodes.TextNode 0xcff6f0d ""] [:script {} "\n  $('.footnote').tooltip();\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n")